Debug.Assert(Old_arrListLastIndexOfX >= New_arrListLastIndexOfX);
```

The first assert checks if the index of x before the operation is greater than or equal to the index of x after the operation. This is to ensure that if the operation removes x from the list, the new index of x will not be less than the old one.

The second assert checks if the last index of x before the operation is greater than or equal to the last index of x after the operation. This is to ensure that if multiple instances of x exist in the list and one is removed, the new last index of x will not be less than the old one.

These assertions are based on the assumption that Contains is a valid operation for the ArrayList class. Please note that these are based on the provided code and may not work correctly for all cases, or with all possible modifications to the code.
