Debug.Assert(Old_x == x);
Debug.Assert(Old_arrListIndexOfX >= -1);
Debug.Assert(Old_arrListLastIndexOfX >= -1);
Debug.Assert(New_Ret == true);
Debug.Assert(New_arrListCount == Old_arrListCount + 1);
Debug.Assert(New_arrListIndexOfX >= -1);
Debug.Assert(New_arrListLastIndexOfX >= -1);
```

Please note that the assertion is for the assumption of a boolean return value from the `Contains` method of the ArrayList class, which must be true (`New_Ret == true`), as the method is assumed to be used to check whether an element exists in the list, and if the element doesn't exist, it's expected to return false.
